{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
As [G]I was a-walking
Down Paradise [D]Street,
To me [D]way, hey, blow the man [G]down!
A [G]pretty young damsel
I chanced for to [D]meet,
Give me [D]some time to blow the man [G]down!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Oh, [G]blow the man down, bullies,
Blow the man [D]down,
To me [D]way, hey, blow the man [G]down!
Oh, [G]blow the man down, bullies,
Blow him a[D]way,
Give me [D]some time to blow the man [G]down!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
She was [G]round in the counter
And bluff in the [D]bow,
To me [D]way, hey, blow the man [G]down!
So I [G]took in all sail
And cried, "Way enough [D]now!"
Give me [D]some time to blow the man [G]down!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
I [G]hailed her in English,
She answered me [D]clear,
To me [D]way, hey, blow the man [G]down!
"I'm [G]from the Black Arrow,
Bound to the Shake[D]speare."
Give me [D]some time to blow the man [G]down!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
